#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:2
msgid ":mod:`!tkinter.ttk` --- Tk themed widgets"
msgstr ":mod:`!tkinter.ttk` --- Widgets med Tk-tema"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:9
msgid "**Source code:** :source:`Lib/tkinter/ttk.py`"
msgstr "**Källkod:** :source:`Lib/tkinter/ttk.py`"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:15
msgid ""
"The :mod:`!tkinter.ttk` module provides access to the Tk themed widget set, "
"introduced in Tk 8.5. Its widgets adapt their appearance to the platform's "
"native theme, giving an application a better and more consistent look and "
"feel than the classic :mod:`tkinter` widgets, whose appearance is fixed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:21
msgid ""
"The basic idea for :mod:`tkinter.ttk` is to separate, to the extent "
"possible, the code implementing a widget's behavior from the code "
"implementing its appearance."
msgstr ""
"Grundtanken med :mod:`tkinter.ttk` är att i möjligaste mån separera den kod "
"som implementerar en widgets beteende från den kod som implementerar dess "
"utseende."

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:25
msgid ""
"Ttk widgets are used just like the classic :mod:`tkinter` widgets and share "
"the same machinery: the widget hierarchy, the geometry managers, variable "
"coupling and event binding. Those foundational concepts are covered in the :"
"mod:`tkinter` documentation and are not repeated here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:36
msgid ""
"`Tk Widget Styling Support (TIP #48) <https://tip.tcl-lang.org/48.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:37
msgid ""
"The Tcl Improvement Proposal that introduced the themed widget styling "
"engine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:41
msgid "Using Ttk"
msgstr "Använda Ttk"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:43
msgid "To start using Ttk, import its module::"
msgstr "För att börja använda Ttk importerar du dess modul::"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:45
msgid "from tkinter import ttk"
msgstr "from tkinter import ttk"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:47
msgid ""
"To override the basic Tk widgets, the import should follow the Tk import::"
msgstr ""
"För att åsidosätta de grundläggande Tk-widgetarna bör importen följa Tk-"
"importen::"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:49
msgid ""
"from tkinter import *\n"
"from tkinter.ttk import *"
msgstr ""
"from tkinter import *\n"
"from tkinter.ttk import *"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:52
msgid ""
"That code causes several :mod:`tkinter.ttk` widgets (:class:`Button`, :class:"
"`Checkbutton`, :class:`Entry`, :class:`Frame`, :class:`Label`, :class:"
"`LabelFrame`, :class:`Menubutton`, :class:`OptionMenu`, :class:"
"`PanedWindow`, :class:`Radiobutton`, :class:`Scale`, :class:`Scrollbar` and :"
"class:`Spinbox`) to automatically replace the Tk widgets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:61
msgid ""
"Overriding the classic widgets with ``from tkinter.ttk import *`` is "
"convenient for adapting existing code, but new code is usually clearer if it "
"imports the module as ``from tkinter import ttk`` and refers to the themed "
"widgets explicitly, such as ``ttk.Button``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:67
msgid ""
"This has the direct benefit of using the new widgets which gives a better "
"look and feel across platforms; however, the replacement widgets are not "
"completely compatible. The main difference is that widget options such as "
"``fg``, ``bg`` and others related to widget styling are no longer present in "
"Ttk widgets. Instead, use the :class:`ttk.Style <Style>` class for improved "
"styling effects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:76
msgid "Ttk widgets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:78
msgid ""
"Ttk comes with 18 widgets, twelve of which already existed in tkinter: :"
"class:`Button`, :class:`Checkbutton`, :class:`Entry`, :class:`Frame`, :class:"
"`Label`, :class:`LabelFrame`, :class:`Menubutton`, :class:`PanedWindow`, :"
"class:`Radiobutton`, :class:`Scale`, :class:`Scrollbar`, and :class:"
"`Spinbox`. The other six are new: :class:`Combobox`, :class:`Notebook`, :"
"class:`Progressbar`, :class:`Separator`, :class:`Sizegrip` and :class:"
"`Treeview`. All of them are subclasses of :class:`Widget`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:86
msgid ""
"Using the Ttk widgets gives the application an improved look and feel. As "
"discussed above, there are differences in how the styling is coded."
msgstr ""
"Genom att använda Ttk-widgetar får programmet ett bättre utseende och en "
"bättre känsla. Som diskuterats ovan finns det skillnader i hur stylingen "
"kodas."

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:89
msgid "Tk code::"
msgstr "Tk-kod::"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:91
msgid ""
"l1 = tkinter.Label(text=\"Test\", fg=\"black\", bg=\"white\")\n"
"l2 = tkinter.Label(text=\"Test\", fg=\"black\", bg=\"white\")"
msgstr ""
"l1 = tkinter.Label(text=\"Test\", fg=\"black\", bg=\"white\")\n"
"l2 = tkinter.Label(text=\"Test\", fg=\"black\", bg=\"white\")"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:95
msgid "Ttk code::"
msgstr "Ttk-kod::"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:97
msgid ""
"style = ttk.Style()\n"
"style.configure(\"BW.TLabel\", foreground=\"black\", background=\"white\")\n"
"\n"
"l1 = ttk.Label(text=\"Test\", style=\"BW.TLabel\")\n"
"l2 = ttk.Label(text=\"Test\", style=\"BW.TLabel\")"
msgstr ""
"style = ttk.Style()\n"
"style.configure(\"BW.TLabel\", foreground=\"black\", background=\"white\")\n"
"\n"
"l1 = ttk.Label(text=\"Test\", style=\"BW.TLabel\")\n"
"l2 = ttk.Label(text=\"Test\", style=\"BW.TLabel\")"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:103
msgid ""
"For more information about TtkStyling_, see the :class:`Style` class "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"För mer information om TtkStyling_, se :class:`Style`-klassdokumentation."

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:107
msgid "Widget"
msgstr "Widget"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:109
msgid ""
":class:`ttk.Widget <Widget>` defines standard options and methods supported "
"by Tk themed widgets and is not supposed to be directly instantiated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:114
msgid "Standard options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:116
msgid "All the :mod:`!ttk` Widgets accept the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:121 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:157
#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:183 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:226
#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:335 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:428
#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:510 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:536
#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:708 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:780
#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:850 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:911
#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:939
msgid "Option"
msgstr "Alternativ"

#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:121 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:157
#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:183 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:226
#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:242 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:335
#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:428 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:510
#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:536 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:708
#: ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:780 ../../library/tkinter.ttk.rst:850
